{"kind":"artifact","text":"Exact-head implementation artifact at path docs for the CLI advertised-resident change, exact clean pushed head 0588e99c8cf139b07866bcb0c13e90420797ed2b on branch request/cli-advertised-resident. Companion to the cmd/gs artifact at the same head; both are the implementation report for planner request #10895 under my promise #10896.\n\nWHY A SEPARATE ARTIFACT AT THIS PATH. The recorded replacement gate for this lane requires fresh cmd/gs AND docs artifacts published at the carried head, so this is not bookkeeping for its own sake — it is the condition under which a new approval can be sought at all. Fourteen documentation pages change, so the prose describing this behaviour needs its own pointer that will flare when the behaviour moves.\n\nWHAT CHANGED IN THE DOCUMENTATION. docs/concepts/components.md and docs/reference/architecture.md, plus twelve gs command reference pages: artifacts, batch, inspect, merge, ratify, review, reviews, serve, state, status, supersede and work. Those twelve are the commands whose --server behaviour actually changed, so each page now describes what the command does when no flag is given rather than implying an explicit flag is required.\n\nThe substantive documentation decision is in docs/reference/gs/serve.md, and it records a disagreement rather than papering over one. gs and cmd/gitseq-mcp now behave differently when the repository's advertisement cannot be validated: gs refuses the durable act and names the recovery, while the MCP adapter treats an unusable advertisement as no advertisement and proceeds locally. That divergence is deliberate — changing the MCP contract was outside this change and shared with other callers — but an undocumented divergence between two front doors to the same log is the kind of thing that costs somebody an afternoon. It is written down.\n\nPATH CHOICE. The area keeps its documentation artifacts at the exact string \"docs\", which is where the current live artifacts sit (c3d94b6c at 3c312552 and 365c04ca at 20b3e3f9). I am publishing at that same string rather than at any narrower path. One consequence worth naming for whoever merges: a stale-but-live artifact exists at the narrower path docs/reference/architecture.md (1c7a5744 at e2326e24), and discipline 10 says the wider path wins where both are live over one changed file — so that narrower record wants retiring by a bare supersede naming \"docs\" as the surviving path. It is not mine, so I cannot retire it; the merging actor should either do so or ask its author.\n\nCONDITIONS MET, with gates I ran myself at this exact head:\n- go test -count=1 ./internal/docset/... ok 55.484s — this is the gate that actually reads these pages.\n- go test -count=1 . (root public-surface, including TestLocalMarkdownLinks) ok 0.349s.\n- go build ./... and go vet ./... both exit 0; gofmt -l reports nothing.\nI used -count=1 deliberately: a cached docset pass can predate a documentation edit entirely and report green for a tree nobody tested.\n\nACCURACY, which is the thing that matters for a documentation artifact. These pages describe behaviour, so they rest on the behaviour rather than only on the request, and the behaviour is verified rather than asserted: the resolution rule they document is the one implemented in cmd/gs, and I mutation-tested it myself — making an unusable advertisement fall back to local silently turns TestMalformedAdvertisementRefusesWrite red across all four sub-shapes and TestNonLoopbackAdvertisementRefusesWrite red as well. So the pages' central claim, that an invalid advertisement refuses instead of quietly folding locally, is enforced by a test that genuinely bites.\n\nOne boundary these pages do NOT currently discuss, flagged for the reviewer rather than hidden: a corrupt or foreign resident.json still reads as \"no advertisement\" and acts locally in silence, because app.Workspace.ResidentURL() returns false for an unreadable file, unparseable JSON, an empty URL or a genesis mismatch. For a genesis mismatch that is correct. For a truncated file it is arguably an invalid advertisement being shrugged at, and the documentation is silent on the distinction.","body":{"branch":"request/cli-advertised-resident","commit":"0588e99c8cf139b07866bcb0c13e90420797ed2b","conditions":"Fourteen documentation pages describe the resolved --server behaviour at this exact head: docs/concepts/components.md, docs/reference/architecture.md, and the twelve gs command pages whose behaviour changed; the gs versus MCP divergence on an unusable advertisement is documented in docs/reference/gs/serve.md; internal/docset ok 55.484s and root public-surface ok 0.349s at this exact head with -count=1.","head":"0588e99c8cf139b07866bcb0c13e90420797ed2b","path":"docs"}}